            <div xml:id="d669">

                <pb facs="1072" n="936" sameAs="frus:frus1888p1/pg936"/>

                <head>No. 669.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Rives to Mr. Thompson.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1888-10-31"><hi rendition="#italic">October</hi> 31,
                        1888</date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 56.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: As you will perceive by the inclosed copy
                    of correspondence I had with Mr. Goutier, consul at Cape Haytien, the Department
                    has been constrained to correct his recent repetition of the error into which he
                    fell, in October, 1885, of announcing to the consular agents within his
                    jurisdiction that “the United States Government does not recognize the right of
                    asylum in consulates for political refugees.”</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">G. L. Rives</hi>,<lb/><hi
                            rendition="#italic">Assistant Secretary.</hi></signed></closer>









